Weight load in ~33 s instead of 420-470 s (SGLANG_LOAD_PREFAULT=1, set by start.sh when FAST_LOAD=1, the default).

On the Spark (GB10, CUDA 13, driver 580) a host-to-device copy from mmap'd safetensors pages that the process has not
touched yet runs at ~0.15 GB/s (10 ms for a 1.5 MB expert tensor), even with the file in the page cache; from touched or
anonymous pages it runs at 37-44 GB/s (tools/copy_bench.py). Stock SGLang copies straight from untouched mmap views, so
the 113,047 tensors of the 68 GB target loaded in 420-470 s with the loading thread inside cuMemcpyHtoDAsync.

- weight_utils.py: the loader workers (num_threads=2 in start.sh: two shards in flight beside the one being copied) read
  their shard sequentially into the page cache (5.6 GB/s instead of ~0.4 GB/s through page faults) and touch its pages;
  the iterator hands tensors of 64 KiB and more out as anonymous copies (165 s -> 33 s against touched mmap pages).
- loader.py: after the model is loaded, every shard's page cache is dropped (posix_fadvise DONTNEED) and malloc_trim
  runs. The per-shard drop during the load frees nothing while live tensors still map the shard, and on this
  unified-memory box SGLang sizes the KV pool from MemAvailable-like free memory: without it up to 40 GB stayed cached.

Cost: the scheduler keeps ~1-2 GB more host memory than after a stock load, so the KV pool is 1.00-1.01M tokens instead
of 1,048,600 (four simultaneous ~252K contexts instead of 262K; see README "Boot"). SGLANG_LOAD_PREFAULT=0
(FAST_LOAD=0) restores stock.

